= February 2025 — The count nobody in the coalition wants read aloud

The government has filed notifications by the hundred: the Justice Fund, the
media transfer, the state-company boards, the election that was ordered printed,
the surveillance billing.
[? if reckoning_team_active = 1: KO's reckoning team adds a section of
constitutional-law professors preparing a complaint against the President's own
signatures, on the argument that the laws he signed and the judges he appointed
are the reason none of this can be settled. **Roman Giertych** briefs it
himself.?]
[? if reckoning_team_active = 0: There is no coordinating body and no single
face for any of it; each ministry files its own and reads about the others in
the press.?]

Against that, the column that matters is empty. Nothing has reached a final
verdict. Almost nothing has reached a trial.

The reasons are structural and none of them are a scandal. The prosecutors who
must build these cases were appointed, promoted or protected under **Zbigniew
Ziobro**, and the ones who were not have spent eight years being punished for
it. The courts that would try them contain judges whose appointment the
government itself calls defective, which means a conviction can be attacked on
that ground by the defendant it was obtained against. An ordinary economic-crime
prosecution in Poland takes years, and eight years of government produce more
than one.

[? if reckoning_fugitives >= 2: Two of the principal defendants are outside the
jurisdiction and neither is coming back voluntarily.?]
[? if reckoning_fugitives = 1: One of the principal defendants is outside the
jurisdiction and shows no intention of returning.?]
[? if reckoning_fugitives = 0: The principal defendants are all still in the
country, which is the one advantage this file has and it will not last.?]

Voters were not promised a legal analysis. They were promised that this would
be dealt with, and the government's own chairman of the reckoning is now
publicly demanding acceleration from the ministry that is supposed to be doing
it[? if reckoning_team_active = 1: — the reckoning team's chairman loudest of
all?]. [? if left_in_government = 1: We sit in the cabinet he is demanding it
from.?][? if left_in_government = 0: We are outside the cabinet and can say so
without owning the answer.?]

- @reckoning_triage
- @reckoning_money
- @reckoning_separate_pg
- @reckoning_accelerate

@reckoning_triage
title: Publish a ranked list of the strongest files and abandon the rest
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Fewer cases, better built, and a public admission that most of the notifications were never going anywhere.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The legal team cannot review and rank the files without capacity.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; reckoning_route = "Ranked triage"; reckoning_delivery += 12; reckoning_noise -= 8; giertych_standing -= 6; prosecution_oversight_capacity += 4; judicial_legitimacy += 3; institutional_trust += 3; public_trust += 2; ko_relation -= 4; left_poll_momentum -= 0.15; news_headline = "The Left demands a ranked list of prosecutions and the abandonment of the rest"

We say the sentence nobody in the coalition wants to say: most of these
notifications will never produce a charge, and filing them was a communications
decision. Rank the files by the evidence that exists, staff those, and tell the
public which ones are being dropped and why.

It is an admission of failure delivered fourteen months in, and it will be
clipped by PiS for a year. It is also the only version of this in which
somebody is eventually convicted of something, because the twelve cases that
can be won stop competing for the same six prosecutors.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the ranking

@reckoning_money
title: Follow the money instead of the arrests
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Audits, tax proceedings and asset recovery reach further than a warrant and photograph worse.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: There is no free capacity to build a recovery route across three ministries.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; reckoning_route = "Asset recovery"; reckoning_delivery += 12; reckoning_noise -= 5; giertych_standing -= 3; nik_independence += 3; administrative_reform_pressure += 4; institutional_trust += 4; justice_fund_salience += 6; public_trust += 3; news_headline = "The reckoning moves from warrants to audits, tax proceedings and recovered money"

Criminal responsibility takes a decade. A grant that was awarded outside the
rules can be reclaimed, an unlawfully paid bonus can be taxed, a foundation can
be struck from a register, and a chamber audit can be published while the
witnesses are still alive.

Nobody is detained on television. Money returns to the budget, the record of
what was done becomes official rather than alleged, and every one of those
findings is admissible in the criminal cases that are still crawling.

- @poland_event_queue: Move to the recovery route

@reckoning_separate_pg
title: Separate the Prosecutor General from the Justice Minister
subtitle: Cost: 2 resources. Take the prosecution service permanently out of the hands of whoever holds the ministry — including ours, and including whoever holds it next.
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: A prosecution statute of this size needs two resources of drafting and coalition work.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; reckoning_route = "Independent prosecution statute"; prosecutor_general_separated = 1; reckoning_delivery += 10; reckoning_noise -= 4; giertych_standing -= 8; prosecution_independence += 12; prosecution_command_clarity += 8; constitutional_restraint += 6; institutional_trust += 5; judicial_legitimacy += 4; ko_relation -= 5; public_trust += 2; news_headline = "A statute takes the prosecution service out of the justice minister's hands"

The office that Ziobro used has never stopped being usable. We legislate it
away: a fixed-term Prosecutor General, transparent removal, published written
instructions, and no minister of any party able to lift a telephone about a
named case again.

KO's leadership dislikes it for the honest reason — it disarms the government
they are currently in — and votes for it because opposing it in public is
impossible. The reckoning gets slower and the next reckoning, whoever conducts
it against whom, gets one fewer weapon.

- @poland_event_queue: Table the prosecution statute

@reckoning_accelerate
title: [? if reckoning_team_active = 1: Back Giertych's demand for acceleration?][? if reckoning_team_active = 0: Back the demand for acceleration?]
subtitle: Give the public the pace it was promised, and accept every case that then falls apart in court.
on-arrival: reckoning_route = "Acceleration"; reckoning_delivery -= 6; reckoning_noise += 12; giertych_standing += 10; ko_right_score += 3; ko_social_liberal_share -= 2; ko_classical_liberal_share += 2; government_procedural_restraint -= 6; judicial_legitimacy -= 4; left_poll_momentum += 0.35; pis_poll_momentum -= 0.2; public_trust += 1; institutional_trust -= 4; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_left_ownership += 4; news_headline = "The coalition promises a faster reckoning and more of it"

We stand behind the demand: more charges, sooner, and no more explaining
procedure to people who were robbed. The polling answers within a fortnight and
the coalition finally sounds like it believes its own campaign.

Prosecutors under deadline file what they have rather than what they can prove.
Every one of those files will be read by a judge whose appointment this
government disputes, in front of a defendant whose lawyer will say the word
*political* on the first page — and be able to point at this fortnight when
they say it.

- @poland_event_queue: Promise the acceleration

