= February 2025 — Two ledgers, one signature

The first ledger is the one we joined for, and it is not imaginary. Wages,
public services, household security: things that exist in law, that were not
going to exist in a cabinet assembled from the other direction, and that our
organisers can point at in a room full of people who did not vote for this.

The second ledger is the one PiS has been settling with its own electorate, and
the contract does not price it. Curriculum. Textbooks. Which foundations get
public money and which are audited into silence. Who is invited to the ministry
and who is investigated by it. The register of things a coalition partner can
be told are internal ministerial matters.

The **[+ culture_compact_safeguards +]**
[? if culture_compact_safeguards = 1: safeguard we wrote into the contract is?]
[? if culture_compact_safeguards != 1: safeguards we wrote into the contract are?]
doing exactly the work they were designed to do, which is the problem.
[? if culture_compact_safeguards >= 2: They have closed the prosecution service,
the constitutional offices and the social floor to unilateral use. That leaves a
narrower channel through which a party that gave up Ziobro for us has to show
its base that nothing has changed — and a narrower channel carries more
pressure, not less.?]
[? if culture_compact_safeguards < 2: We signed too few of them to close much of
anything. The channel is not narrow. It is most of the state, and the only
reason more has not come through it is that nobody in that cabinet has yet
decided it is worth the argument.?]

Inside our own party the discomfort is not a mood, it is a set of numbers our
own regional secretaries are quoting: **[+ razem_dissent : dissent +]** in
Razem, **[+ progressives_dissent : dissent +]** among the progressives, and a
membership that has spent fourteen months explaining a cabinet photograph to
people who joined to oppose it.

**Przemysław Czarnek**, who ran education and science until 2023 — the HiT
curriculum, the Willa Plus grants, and a body of public statements about LGBT
people that this party has read into the Sejm record more than once — is the
loudest voice in PiS arguing that the leadership has bought a majority and
sold the programme.

- @compact_enforce
- @compact_trade
- @compact_ledger
- @compact_quiet

@compact_enforce
title: Take every culture dispute to the coalition committee with the signed text
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Use the contract as an instrument rather than a defence; the cabinet becomes slower and our signature becomes worth something.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The coalition team cannot service a standing dispute docket.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; culture_compact_response = "Enforcement docket"; culture_current_pressure += 6; culture_current_standing -= 5; minority_safety += 5; public_mood_pending_secular_state_left_ownership += 6; public_mood_pending_secular_state_support += 4; institutional_trust += 3; public_trust += 2; progressive_credibility += 5; razem_dissent -= 6; progressives_dissent -= 5; pis_relation -= 7; government_coalition_dissent += 8; news_headline = "The Left opens a standing enforcement docket against its own cabinet"

Every curriculum circular, every grant list, every ministerial appointment goes
onto a numbered docket and into the coalition committee with the clause it
breaches attached. Nothing is settled by a telephone call between leaders any
more, which is precisely what the leaders liked about the arrangement.

PiS's ministers discover that the safeguards have a procedure behind them. Our
own members discover that the signature bought something enforceable. And the
current around Czarnek acquires the argument it has been waiting for: that the
leadership cannot deliver anything to its own voters while this partner is in
the room.

- @poland_event_queue: Open the docket

@compact_trade
title: Let the curriculum go and bank the wage law
subtitle: The trade this coalition was built to make. It works, it is defensible in a wage negotiation, and it is unrepeatable in front of a teachers' union.
on-arrival: culture_compact_response = "Traded"; culture_current_pressure -= 8; culture_current_standing += 8; far_right_agenda += 5; labor_credibility += 6; household_security += 4; government_delivery += 3; pis_relation += 6; minority_safety -= 5; public_mood_pending_secular_state_left_ownership -= 6; progressive_credibility -= 9; razem_dissent += 12; progressives_dissent += 10; feminist_trust -= 6; public_mood_pending_secular_state_backlash += 7; news_headline = "The Left banks the wage law and lets the curriculum dispute go"

We do not spend the coalition's patience on a textbook. The wage and
public-services package goes through with PiS votes and a government majority,
and it is a better law than anything the other coalition would have produced.

The textbook also goes through. So does the grant list. Teachers who spent 2023
being disciplined by that ministry watch us describe the trade as pragmatism,
and the current inside PiS that wanted the trade learns that this partner will
make it again. That lesson is the expensive part, and it does not appear in
either ledger until somebody tests it.

- @poland_event_queue: Bank the wage law

@compact_ledger
title: Publish both ledgers and let our own members audit the trade
subtitle: State what has been bought and what it cost, in public, before anyone else characterises it. Honest, unflattering, and the only version that survives contact with a congress.
on-arrival: culture_compact_response = "Published ledgers"; culture_current_pressure += 2; public_trust += 4; institutional_trust += 2; progressive_credibility += 6; party_unity += 5; movement_autonomy += 4; razem_dissent -= 8; progressives_dissent -= 7; coalition_blur -= 7; left_poll_momentum -= 0.25; pis_relation -= 3; news_headline = "The Left publishes what the cross-bloc compact has bought and what it has cost"

Two columns, printed together, with numbers in both. Wage floors, service
guarantees, the housing programme — against the curriculum, the grants, the
appointments and the disputes we lost. No adjectives.

It is a document that hands PiS a fortnight of quotations and Razem a permanent
reference. It also means that whatever this cabinet does next, we will not be
the party that discovered its own record from a journalist, and our congress
will be arguing about a page rather than about a feeling.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish both ledgers

@compact_quiet
title: Keep the disagreement inside the cabinet
subtitle: Protect the coalition's working temperature and let the culture disputes be settled where nobody can see them or check them.
on-arrival: culture_compact_response = "Kept quiet"; culture_current_pressure += 4; culture_current_standing += 4; coalition_blur += 8; pis_relation += 5; government_delivery += 2; government_coalition_dissent -= 5; progressive_credibility -= 7; razem_dissent += 9; progressives_dissent += 8; public_trust -= 2; news_headline = "The coalition's culture disputes disappear into the cabinet room"

Our ministers raise it where it should be raised, which is to say where nobody
can verify that it was raised. The temperature stays workable. The delivery
files keep moving.

Fourteen months of that has already produced a party whose own members cannot
tell the difference between a dispute we lost and a dispute we did not have.
Another fourteen will produce one that cannot tell PiS's programme from the
coalition's.

- @poland_event_queue: Raise it in the cabinet room
